# SQ (Associated Persons supplemental qualifiers) study data for the strict `SQ--` token.
#
# ⚠⚠ /data/testdata contains ZERO SQ* datasets — every study there is SUPP-only. Before this
# file the `SQ--` token had no dataset-backed coverage anywhere in the repository, so
# Fix #160's four-independent-tokens contract was unexercised on this family. Control for the
# "zero" claim: the same tree holds 24 SUPP* datasets.
#
# Like SUPPQUAL, an SQ dataset carries RDOMAIN and no DOMAIN column, so
# OperationExecutor.unsplitNameFromData resolves it as "SQ" + RDOMAIN.

dataset SQLB label="Associated Persons Supplemental Qualifiers for LB"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col APID     type=Char label="Associated Persons Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
col QORIG    type=Char label="Origin"
col QEVAL    type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | AP-701-1015 | LBSEQ | 1 | LBTMSHI | Lab Result/Upper Limit of Normal | 0.9 | DERIVED | CLINICAL STUDY SPONSOR
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | AP-701-1023 | LBSEQ | 2 | LBTMSHI | Lab Result/Upper Limit of Normal | 1.0 | DERIVED | CLINICAL STUDY SPONSOR
---

# Split form: the data-derived base is the 4-character SQLB, which strict `SQ--` matches.
dataset SQLBHM label="Associated Persons Supplemental Qualifiers for LB (Hematology)"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col APID     type=Char label="Associated Persons Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
col QORIG    type=Char label="Origin"
col QEVAL    type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | AP-701-1015 | LBSEQ | 3 | LBFAST | Fasting Status | Y | CRF | INVESTIGATOR
---

# ⚑ W4 IS DECIDED (owner 2026-08-07). The history, kept because it explains the shape:
# SDTMIG v3.4 §8.4.2 requires SUPPAPFAMH to be renamed SQAPFAMH. RDOMAIN=APFA makes the
# data-derived base SQAPFA — 6 characters — which strict `SQ--` (SQ + exactly 2) does NOT
# reach either. So the rename does not restore reachability THROUGH `SQ--`; it only moves
# which token fails. ScopeMatcher's javadoc is honest about this ("reached by SQ-- only when
# RDOMAIN yields a 2-character remainder").
#
# ⚑ The resolution is a TOKEN, not a matcher change: `SQAPFA--` is prefix.length()+2 = 8 and
# matches this dataset on the name leg. `firstMatchingDomainEntry` computes that for ANY
# prefix, with no closed list.
#
# ⚠⚠ Wave-13 lane A (edit set E) deliberately authored `SQAPFA--` on ZERO rules, and the reason
# is measured, not cautious. The four rules that name this shape (CDISC-CG0018, CORE-000357,
# CDISC-CG0205, CORE-000293) all check `dataset_name longer_than 8`; `SQAPFA--` matches names
# of EXACTLY 8 characters, and 8 is not longer than 8, so the token is PROVABLY INERT on them —
# it cannot change an outcome on any data, ever. Its sibling `SUPPAPFA--` (8+2 = 10) is not
# inert and WAS authored on those four; see supp-family.cdt. Nothing else in the corpus has a
# reachable SQAPFA* population: /data/testdata carries no SQ* dataset at all, and the SEND rules
# among the `SQ--` carriers cannot see one (SEND has no Associated Persons).
dataset SQAPFAMH label="Associated Persons Supplemental Qualifiers for APFA (Medical History)"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col APID     type=Char label="Associated Persons Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
col QORIG    type=Char label="Origin"
col QEVAL    type=Char label="Evaluator"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | APFA | AP-701-1015 | FASEQ | 1 | FAEVLINT | Evaluation Interval | -P1D | DERIVED | CLINICAL STUDY SPONSOR
---
